B.TN=s(["APFS clone and symlink atomic transaction journal","Automatic mount-state discovery for external NVMe volumes","Safe rollback restore without host IDE restarts","Reclaims 100+ GB of primary internal Mac storage"],t.s)
B.Wb=new A.fh("brew install landxcape/tap/mso","mso status","# 1. Inspect current APFS offload volume and symlinks\n$ mso status\n\n# 2. Run diagnostic health check on external SSD mount state\n$ mso diagnose\n\n# 3. Atomically offload Android/Gradle/Xcode developer caches\n$ mso offload --target ~/.android\n$ mso offload --target ~/.gradle/caches\n\n# 4. Atomic rollback restore if external drive needs to be unmounted\n$ mso restore --target ~/.android","Modern mobile and web development tools (Xcode CoreSimulator, Gradle caches, Android AVDs) accumulate hundreds of gigabytes on macOS internal NVMe drives. mac-sym-offload (mso) solves SSD exhaustion by establishing transactional APFS symlink offloads to external high-speed storage. Built in Rust with atomic rollback journals, it guarantees that directory swaps and re-links never corrupt active IDE state even during sudden drive disconnects.",B.TN,"mso status","brew tap landxcape/tap")
B.TK=s(["SIMD-accelerated RGB to ANSI color quantization (< 2ms/frame)","Zero-allocation memory stdout buffer supporting up to 60 FPS streaming","Hardware-accelerated frame decode via native FFmpeg bindings","Supports 16-color, 256-color, and 24-bit TrueColor terminal profiles"],t.s)
B.W1=new A.fh("brew install landxcape/tap/camgylph","camgylph --fps 30","# 1. Stream live webcam feed rendered as ANSI glyphs in terminal\n$ camgylph --device 0 --fps 30\n\n# 2. High-fidelity 24-bit TrueColor ASCII matrix mode\n$ camgylph --color-mode truecolor --contrast 1.2\n\n# 3. Stream ANSI escape sequences directly into a file or pipe\n$ camgylph --fps 60 --record ./stream.ansi","Real-time terminal video rendering typically encounters severe latency bottlenecks due to per-pixel escape code formatting and terminal stdout I/O overhead. camgylph pipelines raw camera frames through hardware FFmpeg decoders, computes color quantization using SIMD vectorized Euclidean distance against ANSI palettes, and streams output via double-buffered memory chunks with configurable frame rate caps (defaulting to 30 FPS, scalable up to 60 FPS) to prevent terminal stdout buffer saturation.",B.TK,"camgylph --device 0 --fps 30","brew tap landxcape/tap")
B.SZ=s(["Raw Ethernet frame crafting for line-speed Layer 2 ARP discovery","Non-blocking asynchronous TCP port probing (65k ports in sub-seconds)","Self-contained static binary with zero external dynamic dependencies","Clean CLI formatting and machine-readable JSON streaming"],t.s)
B.W0=new A.fh("brew install landxcape/tap/rscan","rscan arp 192.168.1.0/24","# 1. Broadcast Layer 2 ARP scan across local subnet\n$ rscan arp 192.168.1.0/24\n\n# 2. High-speed multi-threaded TCP port scan (65k ports in < 2s)\n$ rscan tcp 192.168.1.1 --ports 1-65535 --threads 128\n\n# 3. Emit machine-readable telemetry JSON stream\n$ rscan tcp 10.0.0.1 --ports 80,443,8080 --json | jq .","Network reconnaissance tools either rely on slow sequential socket connections or require heavy multi-megabyte C libraries. rscan is a fast, zero-dependency network scanner written in Rust. It crafts raw L2 Ethernet frames directly for microsecond ARP sweeps and utilizes an asynchronous, non-blocking epoll/kqueue event loop to probe thousands of TCP ports simultaneously without thread exhaustion.",B.SZ,"rscan arp 192.168.1.0/24","brew tap landxcape/tap")
B.Tu=s(["Microsecond monotonic clock synchronization (< 500\xb5s drift)","Adaptive jitter buffer dynamically absorbs Wi-Fi latency spikes","UDP multicast transport prevents local network broadcast storms","Zero pitch-warping phase adjustment algorithm"],t.s)
B.W3=new A.fh("brew install landxcape/tap/synkrophase","synkrophase daemon","# 1. Start master clock synchronization daemon on host\n$ synkrophase daemon --bind 0.0.0.0:4848\n\n# 2. Lock client audio playback engine to master beacon\n$ synkrophase sync --master 192.168.1.100:4848 --latency-target 15ms\n\n# 3. Inspect real-time jitter, phase drift, and buffer metrics\n$ synkrophase status --watch","Distributing multi-room audio over standard Wi-Fi networks results in phase cancellation and audible echo due to clock oscillator divergence and asymmetric network jitter. synkrophase implements a precision PTP-inspired monotonic clock protocol over low-overhead UDP multicast. By calculating round-trip phase delta and dynamically modulating an adaptive micro-sample jitter buffer, it maintains sub-millisecond audio alignment across disparate consumer hardware.",B.Tu,"synkrophase daemon --bind 0.0.0.0:4848","brew tap landxcape/tap")
B.Vz=new A.bc(B.zg,[B.Wb,B.W1,B.W0,B.W3],t.G_)
